      "content": "Thanks, but these rebuttals are way too polite. This is for a high-stakes tournament, not a classroom discussion. In a real debate, the opposition won't just say \"it's too expensive,\" they're going to argue that UBI is a mathematical impossibility that will trigger hyperinflation and destroy the incentive to participate in society entirely.\n\nI need you to move past the \"on the one hand, on the other hand\" approach. If you were looking at the skeptical side of this, what are the actual, most aggressive economic arguments that make the UBI position look fundamentally flawed or even reckless? Give me the arguments that actually make people's blood boil during a debate.",
